WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.867 --> 00:00:15.157
Heidi was staring with wild eyes and trembling from head to foot.

2
00:00:15.158 --> 00:00:18.874
"Heidi, what is going on?" asked Clara's father.

3
00:00:18.875 --> 00:00:21.002
"Why did you come down here?"

4
00:00:21.003 --> 00:00:27.438
White with terror, and hardly able to speak, Heidi answered, "I don't know."

5
00:00:27.439 --> 00:00:32.338
The doctor quickly stepped in and helped Heidi up to bed.

6
00:00:32.339 --> 00:00:34.324
"Don't be frightened, child.

7
00:00:34.325 --> 00:00:36.718
It's all right," he told her.

8
00:00:36.719 --> 00:00:41.561
The doctor settled Heidi into her bed and stayed with her until she stopped shaking.

9
00:00:41.562 --> 00:00:46.317
Then he asked, "Now tell me, where were you going?"

10
00:00:46.318 --> 00:00:49.214
"Nowhere," answered Heidi.

11
00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:52.475
"I didn't know that I'd gone downstairs.

12
00:00:52.476 --> 00:00:54.337
I was just there."

13
00:00:54.338 --> 00:00:56.661
"Had you been dreaming?"

14
00:00:56.662 --> 00:00:59.937
"Yes, I dream every night.

15
00:00:59.938 --> 00:01:03.433
I think I am back in Grandfather's hut.

16
00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:10.143
I wonder if the stars are shining, so in my dream I get up and open the door to the hut.

17
00:01:10.144 --> 00:01:15.620
It's so beautiful, but when I wake up I am still in Frankfurt,"

18
00:01:15.621 --> 00:01:19.818
said Heidi, struggling to keep back the tears.

19
00:01:19.819 --> 00:01:23.913
"And where did you live with your Grandfather?" asked the doctor.

20
00:01:23.914 --> 00:01:26.894
"Up the mountain," said Heidi,

21
00:01:26.895 --> 00:01:34.359
"It is beautiful there," and then she broke into violent weeping.

22
00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.660
"There, there. Go ahead and cry.

23
00:01:37.661 --> 00:01:40.842
It will do you good. Don't worry.

24
00:01:40.843 --> 00:01:43.625
Tomorrow everything will be all right."

25
00:01:43.626 --> 00:01:48.683
The doctor left her quietly and went downstairs to Herr Sesemann.

26
00:01:48.684 --> 00:01:53.873
"First," said the doctor, "let me tell you that Heidi was sleepwalking.

27
00:01:53.874 --> 00:01:57.276
Second, she is consumed by homesickness.

28
00:01:57.277 --> 00:02:00.026
It looks as if she has lost a lot of weight.

29
00:02:00.027 --> 00:02:02.534
She is practically a skeleton.

30
00:02:02.535 --> 00:02:04.497
There is only one remedy.

31
00:02:04.498 --> 00:02:07.996
You must send her home to her mountain."

32
00:02:07.997 --> 00:02:11.585
Herr Sesemann rose and paced up and down the room.

33
00:02:11.586 --> 00:02:14.092
His face was pale with concern.

34
00:02:14.093 --> 00:02:19.923
The next morning, the maid surprised Heidi by telling her to put on her best clothes.

35
00:02:19.924 --> 00:02:25.575
When Heidi was ready, she went downstairs and found Herr Sesemann and Clara in the study.

36
00:02:25.576 --> 00:02:28.427
"Well, what do you say about this, Heidi?

37
00:02:28.428 --> 00:02:33.046
I've decided that you are going home!" said Clara's father.

38
00:02:33.047 --> 00:02:37.378
"Home?" Heidi's face turned rosy with delight.

39
00:02:37.379 --> 00:02:39.660
She couldn't believe her ears.

40
00:02:39.661 --> 00:02:45.018
"Oh, yes, yes, home! I want to go home."

41
00:02:45.019 --> 00:02:50.679
"All right then," said Clara's father, "your carriage is waiting outside.

42
00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:55.756
Say your good-byes to Clara and Sebastian will escort you to Dorfli."

43
00:02:55.757 --> 00:02:59.143
Heidi felt sad about saying good-bye to Clara.

44
00:02:59.144 --> 00:03:04.012
The girls hugged each other, and Clara promised to visit Heidi as soon as she could.

45
00:03:04.013 --> 00:03:10.239
She told Heidi she had filled a small suitcase with dresses and pretty scarves for her.

46
00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:15.685
Then she handed Heidi a basket with 12 fresh rolls for Grannie wrapped in a cloth.

47
00:03:15.686 --> 00:03:22.452
Heidi's delight and sorrow were so evenly mixed that she smiled with tears sparkling in her eyes.

48
00:03:22.453 --> 00:03:29.478
She bundled her favorite book and old straw hat in her red shawl and added them to the basket.

49
00:03:29.479 --> 00:03:34.495
Heidi was lifted into the carriage, and Sebastian took his place beside her.

50
00:03:34.496 --> 00:03:39.941
Herr Sesemann lifted her suitcase up beside her and handed Heidi a small thick packet.

51
00:03:39.942 --> 00:03:42.149
"Keep this package safe, Heidi.

52
00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:45.474
It is a present for you and a letter for your grandfather."

53
00:03:45.475 --> 00:03:50.499
Heidi thanked him with all her heart and hid the present in her basket.

54
00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:53.837
Soon, they were on the way to the train station.

55
00:03:53.838 --> 00:03:59.121
Throughout the train ride, Heidi held tightly to her basket with the precious rolls.

56
00:03:59.122 --> 00:04:07.687
The next day, when they got down from the train, the baker from Dorfli was at the station, loading sacks onto his cart.

57
00:04:07.688 --> 00:04:14.620
Sebastian asked him to take Heidi and her things to Dorfli, and she climbed up onto the seat of his cart.

58
00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:19.933
As the cart headed up the road, Heidi watched Sebastian waving from behind.

59
00:04:19.934 --> 00:04:25.680
Then she turned to face the mountain, trembling with excitement.
